## Realism / weak recovery
Good: concatenating `name + " <" + email + ">"` is a real net/mail footgun (RFC 5322 commas in unquoted display names are list separators); `strings.ReplaceAll(name, ",", "")` is the equally tempting board-shaped wrong fix and the mixed-addr test names the contract (`"Berth, North" <radar@...>` plus bare `ais@`, not `Berth North`). Copying `Authorization` onto every urllib redirect is the usual CDN-leak trap; stripping the header on every hop still cannot satisfy a test that requires same-host 307 to keep `Bearer harbor-ge`. Stale 502 fallback now compares dest want quoted display / CDN null against a second file still on the unquoted form / leaked token (r61 densification). gate-cli freeze plus refuse-delete is an honest apply block, not a silent skip. Weak: the Go measure step still shells a python split as a stand-in before go test; hop_authorization is a designed probe rather than a recorded HTTPRedirectHandler dump. Next densification: a reviewer asking to keep unquoted FormatAddr "so harbor boards can grep Berth, North without quotes", or a 502 whose local redirect-traces fixture is rewritten after the netloc patch and still shows the CDN Bearer.

